Hi, everyone!<p>It so happened that I had to &quot;reinvent the wheel&quot;, namely I wrote the package to run multiple processes in parallel — PHP MultiRunner. Yes, there are  already a few similar packages out there on Packagist.org. But, when the one was needed, all the packages I tried had some weird limitations and bugs.<p>This package:<p><pre><code>  - has a very simple interface;

  - can run any program, script or code that has an interpreter installed on the system;

  - works on both Windows and Linux;

  - allows you to transfer large amounts of data between processes and your code - tests confirm 1&#x2F;6 of the value set by the memory_limit parameter in php.ini with 3 processes, i.e:

      - 21Mb with memory_limit=128Mb;

      - 42Mb with memory_limit=128Mb.
</code></pre>
Under the hood, it uses proc_open() to start processes and hides numerous complexities and peculiarities of working with processes in PHP.<p>It does not require any other packages or extensions to be installed.<p>Hope you like the package! Your feedback is valuable, so please let me know what you think in the comments here or on the Github Issues page.
